	<p>
		I’m a Software Engineer based in Kerala, India. My life is a high-speed
		pursuit of a "good life" as a son, husband, and father, though I’m
		currently losing the race against the clock—there is simply never enough
		time.
	</p>

	<h2>The "Lazy" Engineer Philosophy 🛠️</h2>
	<p>
		I identify as a "lazy" person, but in the most productive way possible:
		I am obsessed with settling problems once and for all. If I have to do
		it twice, I’ll spend three hours automating it so I never have to think
		about it again. I’m an open-source contributor and deeply obsessed with
		the web, though I keep my cognitive overhead low. I have a strict
		"5-item buffer"—I don't hold more than five things in my mind at once,
		and honestly, I don't want to.
	</p>

	<h2>The Tech Stack & The Rivalries 💻</h2>
	<p>
		My setup is a study in irony. I’m deep in the Google ecosystem, yet I
		use a Mac for personal projects (while maintaining a healthy hatred for
		the rest of Apple’s "nonsense"). I ironically still use Windows—which is
		absolute bullshit these days—and rely on Ubuntu for the NDA stuff.
	</p>
	<p>
		A hill I will gladly die on? Safari sucks. I’m constantly evaluating my
		tools to ensure they match the pace of my thinking, craving a
		simplicity.
	</p>

	<h2>Gaming & The Champions Club 🎮</h2>
	<p>
		When the code is pushed, I transition into the Warzone Kerala community,
		where I help maintain the ranks. I’m a proud member of Dr Disrespect’s
		Champions Club and a PS5 owner—though the console currently exists in a
		"no-time-to-play" state of limbo. I’m a gamer at heart, even if my
		gaming sessions are currently shorter than a compiler error log.
	</p>

	<h2>Faint Signals & Physics 🌐</h2>
	<p>
		Outside of the terminal, I apply physics to everything around
		me—calculating the inertia of my daily habits and the entropy of my
		desk. I document these explorations on my blog, Faint Signals. I’m also
		strangely obsessed with song lyrics.
	</p>

	<h2>The Core ✨</h2>
	<p>
		At the end of the day, I’m a proud Malayali who values cultural roots
		and clarity. Whether I’m communicating in Malayalam or English, I’m
		looking for the most efficient path to an interesting conversation.
	</p>
